# The audit beside the steps, and the one thing it must not say.
#
# The Playwright case reads the audit's rows and asserts three things: that the
# kind column is the *call* — `locate`, `act`, `read` — and not "surface" on
# every line (P9-F5), that a locate line names what it looked for and whether it
# matched, and that each row has the shape a regular expression describes. The
# first two are sentences now; the third is not, and `checks.yaml` says so.
#
# It needs a run on the screen, which the story above puts there.
story: the audit pane renders the call detail the model carries
  The run audit list should be visible
  The run audit list should contain "locate"
  The run audit list should contain "matched"
  The run audit list should contain "ok"
  No text in the run audit list should contain "surface"

story: the Heal review opens from the palette and offers the runs worth healing
