  Press "Meta+k"
  Click the go to Heal row
  The toolbar title should contain "Heal review"
  The runs worth healing table should be visible
  The proposals table should be visible
  The proposals table should contain "Nothing is written"
  Every control on this screen should have a name
  Every control on this screen should have an id

# The Surface explorer is gone (T15).
#
# Its story lived here and drove a screen that no longer exists: T15 replaced
# the Explorer with the Surfaces screen and removed its four actions and its
# `/surface/:session/*` routes. What it covered — driving a live target, and
# refusing a call with no intent — is covered by the Surfaces screen, whose own
# checks are driven by `evals/self/yam-on-yam` through `yam surface` and the MCP
# tools against the packaged application.

# Pattern 33: the same screen, measured at two widths.
#
# The Record screen's toolbar keeps its title, its select and its buttons at
# 1440 points, and sheds into the palette when the room runs out. What a flow
# can say about that is what is *there*: at 1440 the select and the four
# buttons; at 900 the title and the palette button that the shed actions moved
# into. The external oracle measures the boxes; this one reads the controls.
story: the Record toolbar keeps its title and its select at two widths
  Resize the window to 1440 by 900
  Click the Flows rail item
  Press "Meta+k"
  Click the go to Session row
  The toolbar title should contain "Record review"
  The Gateway select should be visible
  The Stop recording button should be visible
  Resize the window to 900 by 900
  The toolbar title should contain "Record review"
  The Gateway select should be visible
  Resize the window to 1440 by 900

story: a toolbar that runs out of room sheds into the palette
  Resize the window to 1440 by 900
  Click the Flows rail item
  The Flows heading should be visible
  The Record button should be visible
  Resize the window to 720 by 900
  The Search or run a command button should be visible
  Press "Meta+k"
  The command list should be visible
  The go to Flows row should be present
  Press "Escape"
  Resize the window to 1440 by 900

test: the app's palette and its window
  the command palette opens on the chord and lists the registry's actions
  the Record review opens from the palette and chooses its gateway
  the Run screen opens from the palette and shows its own controls
  the audit pane renders the call detail the model carries
  the Heal review opens from the palette and offers the runs worth healing
  the Record toolbar keeps its title and its select at two widths
  a toolbar that runs out of room sheds into the palette
